[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-81096"] :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{MN}$ traversed from the point $M(0,1)$ to the point $N(3,3),$ then ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,dx-y\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=j$ and $b=3\\,i+3\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =j+t(3\\,i+3\\,j-j) \\\\  & =j+t(3\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =3t\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=3t$ and $y(t)=1+2t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=3\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,dx-y\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3t)^{2}\\cdot 3-(1+2t)\\cdot 2\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}27{t}^{2}-2-4t\\,dt \\\\  & ={[9{t}^{3}-2t-2{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[9(1)^{3}-2(1)-2(1)^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124663/selection/e1122882be3ccd3a3d2b1d68d35a0154503fc8f6a613def1d97f79d0c3a01a0d" :answer/id #uuid "33b05ddb-1936-5888-94e4-a7f6dcceb870" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{28}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124663/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" :answer/id #uuid "efe20c14-c8d5-5aa2-a68d-19bce0c21dbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124663/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "1d16e8d5-2fc9-5728-8f85-9514228c5ebc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124663/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "5d758a3c-6efb-53cf-8a6d-8d2c2e70409d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124663/selection/4779448d8b3cc0e5b0a00009e88d6f7d5c03dee41d9946aacd4addd99553ea2a" :answer/id #uuid "bed5af04-b639-5a19-ad11-f4fc0e2ad811" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124663/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9db9f3ad-f022-5fdf-aaa7-3df6990568aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124663/selection/e1122882be3ccd3a3d2b1d68d35a0154503fc8f6a613def1d97f79d0c3a01a0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-124663/selection/e1122882be3ccd3a3d2b1d68d35a0154503fc8f6a613def1d97f79d0c3a01a0d" "q-124663/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" "q-124663/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-124663/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-124663/selection/4779448d8b3cc0e5b0a00009e88d6f7d5c03dee41d9946aacd4addd99553ea2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124663" :question/id #uuid "c66ab2cc-b437-522c-95f7-ced890c4c0c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-124663" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{MN}$ traversed from the point $M(-1,1)$ to the point $N(1,3),$ then ${\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+{x}^{2}\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=-i+j$ and $b=i+3\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =-i+j+t(i+3\\,j-(-i+j)) \\\\  & =-i+j+t(2\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =(2t-1)\\,i+(2t+1)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=2t-1$ and $y(t)=2t+1$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=2\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx+{x}^{2}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+1)^{2}\\cdot 2+(2t-1)^{2}\\cdot 2\\,dt \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+4t+1)+(4{t}^{2}-4t+1)\\,dt \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}8{t}^{2}+2\\,dt \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}4{t}^{2}+1\\,dt \\\\  & =4{[\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4[\\frac{4}{3}+10]-4[0] \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124663/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223ec615-045d-543e-96f4-fec8882bec9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39345/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "cdfd9cbc-15f5-5e69-a738-beb9d51af0cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39345/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "1a290328-ab74-5fc6-b122-2a7f5a194c14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39345/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "eccff55e-6744-5d53-a8d6-a355baa5fddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39345/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "a2807081-7870-545b-bd16-070fb45dea90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39345/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "515af7c4-5bf9-5ded-aadf-f329d9dd3704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39345/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "31064849-f803-5f13-8cff-8fcc2e37b5c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39345/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-39345/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-39345/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-39345/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-39345/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-39345/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39345" :question/id #uuid "f1ae7484-ea92-5605-a7f3-887e13a1b92e" :question/math-academy-id "q-39345" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(1,2)$ to the point $B(3,4),$ then ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+y\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=i+2\\,j$ and $b=3\\,i+4\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =i+2\\,j+t(3\\,i+4\\,j-(i+2\\,j)) \\\\  & =i+2\\,j+t(2\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =(1+2t)\\,i+(2+2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=1+2t$ and $y(t)=2+2t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=2\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+y\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+2t)\\cdot 2+(2+2t)\\cdot 2\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6+8t\\,dt \\\\  & ={[6t+4{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[6(1)+4(1)^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39345/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223ec615-045d-543e-96f4-fec8882bec9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39345"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124652/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "21a468ab-ba8e-591e-9bab-395457ada2a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124652/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "25909ba1-6f86-59f2-bd3c-0c3a45e452bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124652/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "33ed8dea-b63d-5339-8527-ff766218418b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124652/selection/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" :answer/id #uuid "4725bfb8-2f19-5064-a927-31239033d5fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124652/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "b32376b2-3786-549f-baec-80003542576a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124652/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7db8f7c7-0ba5-58ff-9ae2-d70d8eeb2361" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124652/selection/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" :answer-field/choices ["q-124652/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-124652/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-124652/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-124652/selection/95c393685f82efe05ce58fc07554851561d61659fa09076d238e849d9023f203" "q-124652/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124652" :question/id #uuid "fbaa06f9-d9c5-5dd4-bc0b-84638f7db149" :question/math-academy-id "q-124652" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(-1,2)$ to the point $B(1,0),$ then ${\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=-i+2\\,j$ and $b=i.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =-i+2\\,j+t(i-(-i+2\\,j)) \\\\  & =-i+2\\,j+t(2\\,i-2\\,j) \\\\  & =(2t-1)\\,i+(2-2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=2t-1$ and $y(t)=2-2t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=2\\,i-2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)(2-2t)(2)+(-2)\\,dt \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)(2-2t)-1\\,dt \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}-4{t}^{2}+6t-3\\,dt \\\\  & =2{[-\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}+3{t}^{2}-3t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2[-\\frac{4}{3}+3-3]-2[0] \\\\  & =2[-\\frac{4}{3}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124652/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223ec615-045d-543e-96f4-fec8882bec9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124652"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124658/selection/e42bc579c14885a6fa70d2353a0fb29a4e90ef25fb1e4dd806b6c053230dba8e" :answer/id #uuid "9ea099b5-c099-51be-8fd5-aaf11b96505e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{6}-1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124658/selection/d780409a3d45d3a82a75847168f6a677f9a2be98f9a89073c5f5b03faa0b1de7" :answer/id #uuid "b70d35ea-3489-590f-a028-97005a6ad59f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4}-2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124658/selection/45bd238b753cb17648c05a3dc8d352a9832b6faf33a29e5141e22fd5a3fc3530" :answer/id #uuid "c3b8c2d4-75fc-527f-a813-bf50a4569ec3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{6}-3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124658/selection/b4f71116e3cccd180f7f2d48aaf9892c4f71a54912269325283a0bdeb26b8162" :answer/id #uuid "9ca3f345-6e69-5792-8c76-737929ad9182" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{4}-1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124658/selection/cfa4b3ffc2ac67d57a037e61cfbd552dcf5461736e8e4dee0b109c2935b731cc" :answer/id #uuid "dbe66af3-e191-5b00-97a1-d6cc7e5f97d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{6}-1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124658/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb0c2882-e97e-5453-8397-acaa940cbf29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124658/selection/e42bc579c14885a6fa70d2353a0fb29a4e90ef25fb1e4dd806b6c053230dba8e" :answer-field/choices ["q-124658/selection/e42bc579c14885a6fa70d2353a0fb29a4e90ef25fb1e4dd806b6c053230dba8e" "q-124658/selection/d780409a3d45d3a82a75847168f6a677f9a2be98f9a89073c5f5b03faa0b1de7" "q-124658/selection/45bd238b753cb17648c05a3dc8d352a9832b6faf33a29e5141e22fd5a3fc3530" "q-124658/selection/b4f71116e3cccd180f7f2d48aaf9892c4f71a54912269325283a0bdeb26b8162" "q-124658/selection/cfa4b3ffc2ac67d57a037e61cfbd552dcf5461736e8e4dee0b109c2935b731cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124658" :question/id #uuid "1b08d1f5-7765-5429-b7a8-7cd55a476c8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124658" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to the point $B(4,2),$ then ${\\int }_{C}{e}^{x+y}\\,dx-{e}^{x+y}\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=0\\,i+0\\,j$ and $b=4\\,i+2\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =0\\,i+0\\,j+t(4\\,i+2\\,j-(0\\,i+0\\,j)) \\\\  & =4t\\,i+2t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=4t$ and $y(t)=2t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=4\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x+y}\\,dx-{e}^{x+y}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-{e}^{x+y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{4t+2t}(4-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{6t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6t}}{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6(1)}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{6(0)}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6}-1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124658/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223ec615-045d-543e-96f4-fec8882bec9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124658"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81180/selection/10f3c99fed521124d785f5eeba16af64e787bec3dd0cfd5282a7ef128c1cda3e" :answer/id #uuid "895fad76-b934-5759-b9e8-eb2795cf929b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+14\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81180/selection/96de1478f8ec1ed14994e8ba553ff48ab4da806036467da8a4c6ecef9289a57c" :answer/id #uuid "2c5e5836-dd0e-5785-9059-feac98164686" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+16\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81180/selection/186ba7276780d1a91ae21a1c84797d19d62bfa3859aa8aabba59624e1919cbef" :answer/id #uuid "b26d7244-d53d-5176-bc23-8cf797d7953c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+6\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81180/selection/17f336928cbfc26daaa247767aff0ce40a1e780de22af16fe027c08f4c7972ed" :answer/id #uuid "c4538414-d6a8-50e6-b6cb-c9be49da47ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+12\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81180/selection/c6466e0cd2b53f1994eb63b071e809054f54e30045e10d1cf8d73f87e8e87a21" :answer/id #uuid "52bf10ee-8d97-5b66-b418-d02ece93d951" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+10\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81180/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1878c716-d553-5437-b349-b65eac2506bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81180/selection/10f3c99fed521124d785f5eeba16af64e787bec3dd0cfd5282a7ef128c1cda3e" :answer-field/choices ["q-81180/selection/10f3c99fed521124d785f5eeba16af64e787bec3dd0cfd5282a7ef128c1cda3e" "q-81180/selection/96de1478f8ec1ed14994e8ba553ff48ab4da806036467da8a4c6ecef9289a57c" "q-81180/selection/186ba7276780d1a91ae21a1c84797d19d62bfa3859aa8aabba59624e1919cbef" "q-81180/selection/17f336928cbfc26daaa247767aff0ce40a1e780de22af16fe027c08f4c7972ed" "q-81180/selection/c6466e0cd2b53f1994eb63b071e809054f54e30045e10d1cf8d73f87e8e87a21"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81180" :question/id #uuid "6018e40b-260e-515a-8488-5f23215161b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81180" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the parabola $y=\\pi {x}^{2}$ traversed from the point $A(1,\\pi )$ to point $B(2,4\\pi ),$ then ${\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx+3x\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y=\\pi {x}^{2}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+\\pi {t}^{2}\\,j,\\,t\\in [1,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+2\\pi t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx+3x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+3x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+3x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2{t}^{2}})\\cdot 1+3t\\cdot 2\\pi t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+6\\pi {t}^{2}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}1+6\\pi {t}^{2}\\,dt \\\\  & =[t+2\\pi {t}^{3}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[2+2\\pi (2)^{3}]-[1+2\\pi (1)^{3}] \\\\  & =[2+16\\pi ]-[1+2\\pi ] \\\\  & =1+14\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81180/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f04a969-e7e0-592f-b5cd-e92fedb217a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81180"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124668/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2b306380-12f3-5614-b8b7-fe34c676ebf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124668/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0d7c8d35-0d23-52d3-ae82-d7651c95e8db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124668/selection/49b9ee464914b05da889b24a56e026e479c6989f8c7fb611b2828c3fa7d40d87" :answer/id #uuid "e7aa0081-1a85-5f3a-a3d4-cdcbad442a26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{31}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124668/selection/b1791ad9a1ab23a657f0b90288d3a9944a679a82b0981d41da0c52af5a6a321a" :answer/id #uuid "10188e13-a4f5-5171-afa4-0bc547437898" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124668/selection/1a9483841df301d0d8304986bfec9a52b4f49d31cfd2980ff1d8d6f175662caf" :answer/id #uuid "3f5715e0-cebf-5bc4-b486-8793551ea1a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124668/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18e453f1-a564-5187-9aa8-69167b2219cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124668/selection/1a9483841df301d0d8304986bfec9a52b4f49d31cfd2980ff1d8d6f175662caf" :answer-field/choices ["q-124668/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-124668/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-124668/selection/49b9ee464914b05da889b24a56e026e479c6989f8c7fb611b2828c3fa7d40d87" "q-124668/selection/b1791ad9a1ab23a657f0b90288d3a9944a679a82b0981d41da0c52af5a6a321a" "q-124668/selection/1a9483841df301d0d8304986bfec9a52b4f49d31cfd2980ff1d8d6f175662caf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124668" :question/id #uuid "6ae31e0d-1670-5627-83a1-990fa19c67ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-124668" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the graph $y={x}^{3}$ traversed from the point $P(1,1)$ to point $Q(2,8),$ then ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{1}{y}\\,dx+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y={x}^{3}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+{t}^{3}\\,j,\\,t\\in [1,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+3{t}^{2}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{1}{y}\\,dx+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot 3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}+3\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2{t}^{2}}+3t]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{2({2}^{2})}+3(2)]-[-\\frac{1}{2({1}^{2})}+3(1)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}+6+\\frac{1}{2}-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124668/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f04a969-e7e0-592f-b5cd-e92fedb217a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124668"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80983/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "10982d42-77ae-5d0b-9b02-bb5996e7888f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80983/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "4bb41a96-9e95-5bd9-9ecb-c789a06f1bbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80983/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "cfd2b609-63b0-5032-a630-dd9f8e33291d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80983/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "2c24b5cf-5d3a-516d-887d-a0477093b61f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80983/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "510fb5d3-e4a3-57a3-ab8e-e393b878e830" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80983/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe7b7f2b-5561-5947-a10f-a30d4b0c13d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80983/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-80983/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-80983/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-80983/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-80983/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-80983/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80983" :question/id #uuid "d94da7fe-e098-5e66-b337-48ebeb07cbc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-80983" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the graph $y=\\sqrt{x}$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to point $B(1,1),$ then  ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+y)\\,dx+(3x+2y)\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y=\\sqrt{x}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j={t}^{2}\\,i+t\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,1]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=2t\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+y)\\,dx+(3x+2y)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+(3x+2y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(3x+2y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({({t}^{2})}^{2}+t)\\cdot 2t+(3{t}^{2}+2t)\\cdot 1\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{4}+t)\\cdot 2t+3{t}^{2}+2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{t}^{5}+5{t}^{2}+2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{6}}{3}+\\frac{5{t}^{3}}{3}+{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{(1)^{6}}{3}+\\frac{5(1)^{3}}{3}+(1)^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{5}{3}+1]-[0] \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80983/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f04a969-e7e0-592f-b5cd-e92fedb217a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80983"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39679/selection/cff8d7c1bdddd654869332d5d80126176407b72aace8e58d5278702929be052a" :answer/id #uuid "8a09ba1c-f44f-5be5-bb03-48671d45ab73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39679/selection/d510ce22c68bc8da426dd5f45c8357bd50a813be60230828430f55076e04ec51" :answer/id #uuid "293d67a8-4816-59e3-8ba9-3fc0fb08e0a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39679/selection/9c69f016976bf9a71632454fabab6367cb05e79c2c9dc1cffc07c445915c70fd" :answer/id #uuid "e9d3194f-95cb-5134-8a31-4ef0e27b9f90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39679/selection/aed41ef9ece0d984a17e264d7517b6fce48931857cb568f47d7abaf57853e595" :answer/id #uuid "25c2e8b4-e5f6-5d04-9c60-dfc6cbeafb12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4e-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39679/selection/4c023df447c5fd9d0416ebc9d5b1f44a1ed2da11b999d10a9fe991fdafc46a00" :answer/id #uuid "6a0fc824-3cef-5a93-8aaa-5133b3d2abf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39679/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ea448d3-25e0-573c-8ef8-db52b4727248" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39679/selection/d510ce22c68bc8da426dd5f45c8357bd50a813be60230828430f55076e04ec51" :answer-field/choices ["q-39679/selection/cff8d7c1bdddd654869332d5d80126176407b72aace8e58d5278702929be052a" "q-39679/selection/d510ce22c68bc8da426dd5f45c8357bd50a813be60230828430f55076e04ec51" "q-39679/selection/9c69f016976bf9a71632454fabab6367cb05e79c2c9dc1cffc07c445915c70fd" "q-39679/selection/aed41ef9ece0d984a17e264d7517b6fce48931857cb568f47d7abaf57853e595" "q-39679/selection/4c023df447c5fd9d0416ebc9d5b1f44a1ed2da11b999d10a9fe991fdafc46a00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39679" :question/id #uuid "8c9902f1-e71c-5438-8c72-c703b5eef0e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-39679" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ traversed from the point $P(0,0)$ to point $Q(1,1),$ then ${\\int }_{C}4y{e}^{xy}\\,dx+dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,1]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=3{t}^{2}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}4y{e}^{xy}\\,dx+dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4y{e}^{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4y{e}^{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4t\\cdot {e}^{{t}^{3}\\cdot t}\\cdot 3{t}^{2}+1\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}12{t}^{3}{e}^{{t}^{4}}+1\\,dt \\\\  & ={[3{e}^{{t}^{4}}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[3{e}^{(1)^{4}}+(1)]-[3{e}^{(0)^{4}}+(0)] \\\\  & =[3e+1]-[3] \\\\  & =3e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39679/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f04a969-e7e0-592f-b5cd-e92fedb217a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39679"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90871/selection/6acadda2cf01d7393af5cf150300ca180189308ad197cceffca549e1b6e5368c" :answer/id #uuid "8e3136e1-4c21-5c57-bda8-20ae9658cbac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90871/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "c1d579c8-98ab-5754-ab65-280f4c5e2879" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90871/selection/af6b2f75b025fd0301525c16740df7142fa841bfc3244696d2d508c03ede3e42" :answer/id #uuid "d530b69e-1a02-5b16-85b1-05efd5a591cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi +3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90871/selection/ad5f441ebc32c9cbb6453f4d59c36a31c9bd747de66abecedf68987450f5cccd" :answer/id #uuid "95543442-ffaa-5008-a06a-3adf1e6d65d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90871/selection/30d771277e5f88c2a08a4e446b7ea080dd38abbdbbc820f6d698c4b2c0bc77a1" :answer/id #uuid "1ff3abce-659d-522a-bba4-ba2ab70a0013" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90871/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a345b860-5a29-5776-9e58-b438df690f90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90871/selection/ad5f441ebc32c9cbb6453f4d59c36a31c9bd747de66abecedf68987450f5cccd" :answer-field/choices ["q-90871/selection/6acadda2cf01d7393af5cf150300ca180189308ad197cceffca549e1b6e5368c" "q-90871/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" "q-90871/selection/af6b2f75b025fd0301525c16740df7142fa841bfc3244696d2d508c03ede3e42" "q-90871/selection/ad5f441ebc32c9cbb6453f4d59c36a31c9bd747de66abecedf68987450f5cccd" "q-90871/selection/30d771277e5f88c2a08a4e446b7ea080dd38abbdbbc820f6d698c4b2c0bc77a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90871" :question/id #uuid "4f46705e-e884-5e5f-ae5f-c07240ccea0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-90871" :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the parabola $y=\\pi {x}^{2}$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to point $B(1,\\pi ),$ then ${\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}})\\,dx+4{x}^{2}\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y=\\pi {x}^{2}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+\\pi {t}^{2}\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,1]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+2\\pi t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}})\\,dx+4{x}^{2}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+4{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+4{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{{t}^{2}})\\cdot 1+4{t}^{2}\\cdot 2\\pi t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +8\\pi {t}^{3}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}8\\pi {t}^{3}-1\\,dt \\\\  & =[2\\pi {t}^{4}-t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[2\\pi (1)^{4}-1]-[0] \\\\  & =2\\pi -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-90871/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f04a969-e7e0-592f-b5cd-e92fedb217a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90871"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-81192"] :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{y\\,dy-x\\,dx}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},$ where $C$ is part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $C$ is a circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{y\\,dy-x\\,dx}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{y\\cdot {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t-x\\cdot {x}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{y\\cdot {y}^{′}-x\\cdot {x}^{′}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[-1-1] \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124655/selection/7a170d779c869793960dd5744e4098a49371cc8c7e56c688ad64a09aa7bb0592" :answer/id #uuid "26b58c27-7cd2-5ece-90e7-b73d7d369967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}6-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124655/selection/ffcc6d1827d75976dd301f5b361d15490417b36c00cdc773497416245371152f" :answer/id #uuid "7ba1b722-95a9-5959-8aa7-ca081ec72e1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}3-{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124655/selection/3982158b1b9b7463dd246fe0dcc12dfbc790b0a699c8932f9cb756217ca3576f" :answer/id #uuid "e561a44f-6436-51ea-bf08-7d7252a65d84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}6{sin}^{2}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124655/selection/5b59c64bd49580696b1688691f264a8233ea392db324090c41f831353616fc7b" :answer/id #uuid "1d25aef3-6a22-5303-9542-21f46291fc8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124655/selection/9fcd99c0d3537aef6f7b4c0c703dad051bb47f2ef5f58122c0136829a6c35c51" :answer/id #uuid "a7727c98-031b-5925-9a28-0a6d2bb7af1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124655/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "09887d6a-fbca-57c7-bcba-9fc522408947" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124655/selection/7a170d779c869793960dd5744e4098a49371cc8c7e56c688ad64a09aa7bb0592" :answer-field/choices ["q-124655/selection/7a170d779c869793960dd5744e4098a49371cc8c7e56c688ad64a09aa7bb0592" "q-124655/selection/ffcc6d1827d75976dd301f5b361d15490417b36c00cdc773497416245371152f" "q-124655/selection/3982158b1b9b7463dd246fe0dcc12dfbc790b0a699c8932f9cb756217ca3576f" "q-124655/selection/5b59c64bd49580696b1688691f264a8233ea392db324090c41f831353616fc7b" "q-124655/selection/9fcd99c0d3537aef6f7b4c0c703dad051bb47f2ef5f58122c0136829a6c35c51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124655" :question/id #uuid "4adcf258-fc9a-5300-865b-c8efb5f76002" :question/math-academy-id "q-124655" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x-2y)\\,dx+2x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(0,3)$ to the point $B(0,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $3,$ respectively, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x-2y)\\,dx+2x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(x-2y)\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+2x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}((x-2y)\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+2x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t))\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6{sin}^{2}⁡t+6{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}6-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124655/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5b5c517-8e13-5b70-bd1f-15ae495f0632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124655"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124657/selection/53bc1906876979e3eb30227ed7c90127911acd81b09034c81c05eeefc6280b14" :answer/id #uuid "cf66fde9-55a3-5135-9643-6ccae8414fe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+1\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124657/selection/eba6f10afcfec294093f3bbb30c97dc22796fb1453e7f34154ee7382ec6c88ca" :answer/id #uuid "ecd78caa-ff3a-5809-803d-0e02fde09815" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-1\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124657/selection/ce0600cbee5e63379803b40f5329de7461e954c9ef62a588f714db3305b4cdb3" :answer/id #uuid "a6f8cb8f-9eda-56ad-a863-30de44f2e042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-2\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124657/selection/a668e1f8f45f4f10d85d706a8bedffd5f67894896c4a57fbf8b4a3572f93f293" :answer/id #uuid "f9211737-b124-58da-9a96-117402fb0fd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124657/selection/49023229f77158379a7a12e577a13365af200e0273c2f769a87ca9c23a4952b2" :answer/id #uuid "3785352c-2f95-5c6e-adf8-d4a5e7730e48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124657/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "47efcabf-cfeb-57b0-ba13-2bd322cbe7c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124657/selection/eba6f10afcfec294093f3bbb30c97dc22796fb1453e7f34154ee7382ec6c88ca" :answer-field/choices ["q-124657/selection/53bc1906876979e3eb30227ed7c90127911acd81b09034c81c05eeefc6280b14" "q-124657/selection/eba6f10afcfec294093f3bbb30c97dc22796fb1453e7f34154ee7382ec6c88ca" "q-124657/selection/ce0600cbee5e63379803b40f5329de7461e954c9ef62a588f714db3305b4cdb3" "q-124657/selection/a668e1f8f45f4f10d85d706a8bedffd5f67894896c4a57fbf8b4a3572f93f293" "q-124657/selection/49023229f77158379a7a12e577a13365af200e0273c2f769a87ca9c23a4952b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124657" :question/id #uuid "74e17500-b87c-52de-8a8d-2add096034fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-124657" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{2}{y}\\,dx+y{e}^{x}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(1,0)$ to the point $B(0,2).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $2,$ respectively, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{2}{y}\\,dx+y{e}^{x}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2}{y}\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+y{e}^{x}\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{2}{y}\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+y{e}^{x}\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-1\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124657/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5b5c517-8e13-5b70-bd1f-15ae495f0632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124657"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124653/selection/ea62112a38f97fb71bc0b6a4df4589b03779777c79177967f1ee3d903fc2c9a9" :answer/id #uuid "c90e3b8c-9bb9-56c8-ae2f-24ef35b0dc29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+3\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124653/selection/418781ac2b810166bc3c495fc77e7467e0106579682e0da993e03729b6021610" :answer/id #uuid "8bf3f57f-a3e6-571d-a883-4ae3f6691697" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124653/selection/311c54237a4501c6ab42ff758ae7cb8560ae83ad1c409a9def9bc42655351458" :answer/id #uuid "87536d73-0277-5d7a-b387-6f787dad3ec0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124653/selection/16e6d3695f7e74114e9a3bbab2c35e3c790f5e89f275be07c4503e8f3e56721d" :answer/id #uuid "40bc0947-7f94-5cbf-8d3e-3f678c7e5534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+3\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124653/selection/6dd08853ef53f04e1a45acc81eb07b962ca6a812ab8644b7fda90946b2f04229" :answer/id #uuid "b27bac45-3ada-502b-8761-88865b8667d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+1\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124653/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee87988e-aa1b-53c3-a24e-fa242f7d02b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124653/selection/ea62112a38f97fb71bc0b6a4df4589b03779777c79177967f1ee3d903fc2c9a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-124653/selection/ea62112a38f97fb71bc0b6a4df4589b03779777c79177967f1ee3d903fc2c9a9" "q-124653/selection/418781ac2b810166bc3c495fc77e7467e0106579682e0da993e03729b6021610" "q-124653/selection/311c54237a4501c6ab42ff758ae7cb8560ae83ad1c409a9def9bc42655351458" "q-124653/selection/16e6d3695f7e74114e9a3bbab2c35e3c790f5e89f275be07c4503e8f3e56721d" "q-124653/selection/6dd08853ef53f04e1a45acc81eb07b962ca6a812ab8644b7fda90946b2f04229"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124653" :question/id #uuid "c8b59c59-a390-5b22-8421-70bf95742c06" :question/math-academy-id "q-124653" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}({e}^{x}+y)\\,dx-x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=3$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(0,\\sqrt{3})$ to the point $B(-\\sqrt{3},0).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $C$ is a circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at the origin, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({e}^{x}+y)\\,dx-x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({e}^{x}+y)\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(({e}^{x}+y)\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}-x\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({e}^{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-3{sin}^{2}⁡t-3{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-3\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+3\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124653/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5b5c517-8e13-5b70-bd1f-15ae495f0632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124653"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-124597"] :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx-{x}^{2}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(1,0)$ to the point $B(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $C$ is a circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,dx-{x}^{2}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}({y}^{2}\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}-{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{sin}^{3}⁡t-{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡t+{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9515"] :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overline{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to the point $B(1, 1),$ calculate the line integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C x^2y\\,\\mathrm{d}x + xy\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $\\mathbf{a} = 0\\,\\mathbf{i} + 0\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = 1\\,\\mathbf{i} + 1\\,\\mathbf{j}.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =t\\,i+t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0 \\le t \\le 1.$ So, we have that $x(t) = t$ and $y(t) = t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,dx+xy\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\cdot t\\cdot 1+t\\cdot t\\cdot 1\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7038"] :question/problem "If the path $C$ is a part of the parabola $y=x^2$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to the point $B(1,1),$ evaluate the line integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x + (x-y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y = x^2.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,1]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+(x-y)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+(x-y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((x+y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(x-y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(t+{t}^{2})\\cdot 1+(t-{t}^{2})\\cdot 2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}t+3{t}^{2}-2{t}^{3}\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+{t}^{3}-\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}+1-\\frac{1}{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7035"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059731/assets/7a6e67435aab40d5bf3630c66f79241008357e1549b1c77b4c0bdfea2b453883.png)\n\nEvaluate $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C \\dfrac{y\\,\\mathrm{d}x - x\\,\\mathrm{d}y}{x^2+y^2},$ where $C$ is a part of the circle $x^2+y^2=4$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $\\left(0,2\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a parametrization for the given path is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$  is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{′}(t)\\,i+{y}^{′}(t)\\,j=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{y\\,dx-x\\,dy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{y\\cdot {x}^{′}-x\\cdot {y}^{′}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}},dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{-4{sin}^{2}⁡t-4{cos}^{2}⁡t}{4({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{-4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)}{4({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,dt \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,dt \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
